Hi Kathleen and Arjun,

Could we make up just one first-session envelope by Thursday 27 March and che=
ck it together? I've attached Read the invitation at home (HO-001 v1.0) and t=
he session-to-packet list (MAP-001 v1.0).

Please print the first handout on one Letter sheet, double-sided on the long =
edge. Turn it over and check that the invitation and questions on the front a=
nd Check your answers on the back are on the same sheet and face the same way=
. Kathleen and I found the back upside down on our first copy last week, so I=
'd like to see the one set before we make more.

For an absence, Arjun will confirm which session was missed. Kathleen can the=
n use the attached list to select the paper for that session and post it. The=
 list also shows where a two-sheet booklet is needed and the page order.

Thanks both,
Heather

